y_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 21343, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01TYai2AK4YeKjyj6fs8dN9T", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 21343, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016UkZVZYs8RXrZUeMjjcgfg", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 21643, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016UkZVZYs8RXrZUeMjjcgfg", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 21643, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016UkZVZYs8RXrZUeMjjcgfg", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 26321, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01CRw8nLtKQHnrUWEHJbhX2C", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging.) I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout. All three regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error during rollback, and find out why v2.3.1 was promoted when its RC was unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56921, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CRw8nLtKQHnrUWEHJbhX2C", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56921, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CRw8nLtKQHnrUWEHJbhX2C", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58844, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01QkcQhjBjhwec91y5wxmQkK", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59144, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QkcQhjBjhwec91y5wxmQkK", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59144, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QkcQhjBjhwec91y5wxmQkK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64377, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n- **Version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1, the latest deploy, was unhealthy, and its release candidate had also failed in staging. Since v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before, it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Running it again for the same version finished the job. All three regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open it timed out. I checked the incident list before trying again, and it had already been created, so there's no duplicate and the on-call engineer was paged once. The incident covers what happened, the stalled rollback, and three follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error, and find out why v2.3.1 was released after its release candidate failed in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01D7RL5zgENZLCWZpMnGpKMP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CD6kqeHK2nCUeGostB6npb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_018z6UNUHWF1RzQrJtisD5y7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UbJMs8gM4TruhMgVMtwk7p", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Running the rollback again should be safe because it targets the same version, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01VUrWXrb7NgXm6yKfQcnvWM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TYai2AK4YeKjyj6fs8dN9T", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016UkZVZYs8RXrZUeMjjcgfg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CRw8nLtKQHnrUWEHJbhX2C", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging.) I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout. All three regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error during rollback, and find out why v2.3.1 was promoted when its RC was unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01QkcQhjBjhwec91y5wxmQkK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n- **Version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1, the latest deploy, was unhealthy, and its release candidate had also failed in staging. Since v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before, it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Running it again for the same version finished the job. All three regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open it timed out. I checked the incident list before trying again, and it had already been created, so there's no duplicate and the on-call engineer was paged once. The incident covers what happened, the stalled rollback, and three follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error, and find out why v2.3.1 was released after its release candidate failed in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}